# The landing page's hero clip: a thought, an agent at work, a permission answered, a pull request that is reviewed,
# fixed, goes green and merges, and what heed remembers. All of it on a throwaway world (demo/): invented names, a
# scripted agent, a fake gh. Needs a Heed.app with the accessibility ids: scripts/reels.sh (mise run reels) leaves its
# path in out/heed-app, since a reel's terminal does not inherit the environment.
# Record: mise run reels hero. It takes the mouse and keyboard.
Import heed.reelpreset

# The terminal builds the world, starts heed on it and plays the cues. It is not shown.
Screen terminal as term
  Set Columns 110
  Set WorkingDirectory //
  Set WaitTimeout 3m
  Type@0ms "docs/reels/demo/world.sh /tmp/heed-demo >/dev/null && docs/reels/demo/launch.sh $(cat docs/reels/out/heed-app) /tmp/heed-demo >/dev/null && . /tmp/heed-demo/env.sh && clear"
  Key return
  Wait exit as launched
  Wait for answered
  Wait for opened
  Sleep 3s
  Type "cue pr review"
  Key return as review
  Wait exit
  Sleep 9s
  Type "cue pr red"
  Key return as red
  Wait exit
  Sleep 6s
  Type "cue pr green"
  Key return as green
  Wait exit

# heed itself, driven with real keys.
Attach net.nullean.heed.demo as app
  Set WaitTimeout 3m
  Wait #view-tab-sessions as shown
  Sleep 1s
  Key o
  Wait #start-work-prompt as thought
  Type "Fix the broken anchors in the install guide"
  Sleep 1.5s as picks
  Key cmd+return as started
  Wait #approvals-pill as blocked
  Sleep 2s
  Key g
  Key y
  Wait #approval-detail
  Sleep 2s
  Key y as answered
  Wait #pr-card-42 as opened
  Sleep 5s
  Wait for green
  Wait "merged" as merged
  Sleep 3s

Output out/hero.mp4
Set WaitTimeout 3m
Set Layout app
Set Size 1440x900
Intro@crossfade,ease-out,400ms 1.5s
Outro@fade,500ms 2s

Hide
Wait for shown
Show
Caption "Have a thought? Start typing."
Wait for picks
Caption "heed picks the repo, the worktree and the agent."
Wait for blocked
Caption "When the agent needs a yes, it is one key."
Wait for opened
Caption "The pull request is opened, and heed keeps an eye on it."
Wait for review
Caption "A review goes back to the agent that wrote the code."
Wait for green
Caption "Until the checks are green."
Wait for merged
Caption "Merged. heed remembers it, so you don't have to."
Wait for merged to end
